Day 21 – RetailPulse Integrated Business Intelligence Dashboard

Objective

The objective of Day 21 was to develop the final RetailPulse Dashboard using Streamlit by integrating forecasting, inventory optimization, customer churn prediction, customer segmentation, and rolling sales statistics into a unified business intelligence platform.

Dataset Overview

Multiple project datasets were imported into the dashboard, including:

- Hybrid Forecast Results
- Prophet Forecast
- Inventory Optimization Results
- Customer Churn Predictions
- RFM Features
- Rolling Statistics

These datasets were combined to provide a comprehensive view of retail business performance.

Dataset Features

The dashboard utilizes the following information:

- Hybrid Demand Forecast
- Prophet Forecast
- Inventory Recommendations
- Customer Churn Probability
- RFM Customer Metrics
- Rolling Sales Statistics

These datasets support real-time monitoring and business analysis.

Data Preparation

All required CSV files were loaded using Pandas. The dashboard verified dataset availability before generating visualizations and business metrics. The application was configured using Streamlit with a wide layout for an improved user experience.

Dashboard Development

A comprehensive Streamlit application named "RetailPulse Dashboard" was developed. The dashboard integrates all major project modules into a single interactive interface for retail business monitoring.

Forecast Monitoring

The dashboard displays demand forecasting information using both the Hybrid Forecast and Prophet Forecast datasets. Forecast results help users analyze future sales trends and support inventory planning.

Inventory Optimization

Inventory optimization results were integrated into the dashboard to display recommended inventory levels and stock management information, helping businesses reduce stock shortages and overstock situations.

Customer Churn Analysis

Customer churn prediction results were incorporated into the dashboard to identify customers with a high probability of churn. These insights support customer retention strategies.

Customer Segmentation

RFM features were integrated to analyze customer purchasing behavior based on Recency, Frequency, and Monetary values. These metrics enable effective customer segmentation and marketing decisions.

Rolling Sales Analysis

Rolling statistics were included to monitor sales trends over time. These metrics provide insights into business stability, seasonal changes, and demand fluctuations.

Report Generation

The dashboard integrates ReportLab for generating PDF reports summarizing important business metrics and project outcomes. This feature supports automated business reporting.

Application Deployment

The complete dashboard was saved as "app.py" and executed using Streamlit, providing a web-based interactive interface for business intelligence and retail analytics.

Key Findings

• Successfully integrated multiple project datasets into a single dashboard.
• Loaded Hybrid Forecast and Prophet Forecast results.
• Integrated inventory optimization recommendations.
• Displayed customer churn prediction information.
• Included RFM customer segmentation metrics.
• Monitored rolling sales statistics.
• Generated PDF business reports using ReportLab.
• Developed the final RetailPulse Streamlit application.
• Successfully deployed the dashboard using Streamlit.

Conclusion

Day 21 focused on integrating all project modules into the final RetailPulse Business Intelligence Dashboard. The application successfully combines demand forecasting, inventory optimization, customer churn prediction, customer segmentation, rolling sales analysis, and automated report generation into a single interactive platform. The completed dashboard provides a comprehensive solution for retail analytics, business reporting, and strategic decision-making.